  "intro": "قَبْلَ (before) and بَعْدَ (after) go straight before a noun, which takes the -i ending: قَبْلَ الْعَشَاءِ (before dinner), بَعْدَ الدَّرْسِ (after the lesson). Before a whole action, add أَنْ: بَعْدَ أَنْ أَكَلْنَا (after we ate). To tell a story step by step, use أَوَّلًا (first), ثُمَّ (then), بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ (after that) and أَخِيرًا (finally).",
